@NODE iNTRODUCTiON "iNTRODUCTiON OF iMJG VERSiON 1.5"

iCH MUSS JETZT GEHEN VERSiON 1.5 iS PROBALY THE BEST LOGOFF-DOOR ARROUND.
iT HAS @{"FEATURES" LiNK FEATURES} THAT OTHER LOGOFF-DOORS DOESN'T HAVE.

@ENDNODE

@NODE FEATURES "FEATURES OF iMJG VERSiON 1.5"

i DECiDED TO CODE MY OWN LOGOFF-DOOR, BECAUSE WHENEVER i iNSERTED A NEW
NUMBER OF ANY OTHER BBS'S TO MY LOGOFF-SCREEN, THE USERS START CRYiNG,
BECAUSE ALL OF THEM WANT A NUMBER iN MY LOGOFF-SCREEN. AFTER A WHiLE MY
LOGOFF-SCREEN WAS THREE SCREENS LONG. NOW WHEN YOU LOG OFF YOU HAVE THE
OPTiON TO JUMP TO A SPECiAL BBS-LiST WHiCH CAN BE EDiTED BY THE SYSOP.
i ALSO iNCLUDED A SPECiAL GREETiNGS-LiST WHERE THE SYSOP CAN PUT iN HiS
SPECiAL GREETiNGS.

ALL LOGOFF DOORS i HAVE SEEN HAD NO CHAT-OVERiDE-SECURiTY-LEVEL-FUNCTiON.
THAT MEANS EVERY USER WAS ABLE TO PAGE THE SYSOP EVEN iF HE TURNED OFF THE
CHATFLAG. WELL, THiS iS NO BiG iNVENTiON, BUT iT DiFFERS MY DOOR FROM ANY
OTHER LOGOFF-DOOR THAT HAS BEEN OUT YET.

HERE ARE ALL OPTiONS:  - LOGOFF
                       - RELOGON
                       - BACK TO BBS
                       - PAGE SYSOP (WiTH CHAT-OVERiDE-CHECK)
                       - WRiTE COMMENT TO SYSOP
                       - ENTER A MESSAGE                        
                       - BBS-LiST
                       - GREETiNGS


i ALSO ADDED SOME iNFORMATiVE USER STATiSTiCS:
 
1. HOW OFTEN DiD THE USER CALL THE BBS.
2. HOW LONG WAS HE/SHE ON-LiNE TODAY.
3. HOW MUCH TiME DOES HE/SHE HAVE LEFT WHEN HE/SHE CALLS AGAiN TODAY.
4. WHAT iS THE ACTUAL TiME WHEN THE USER iS LOGGiNG OFF.

THAT ALL WiLL BE SHOW BELOW THE NORMAL LOGOFF-MENU iN THiS STYLE:


            THANK YOU MuMu FOR CALLiNG kEY wEST bBS ...            
                                                                   
YOU CALLED THiS SYSTEM 746 TiMES. YOU WERE 3 MiNUTES ON-LiNE TODAY.
                                                                   
    YOU HAVE 1436 MiNUTES LEFT TODAY. iT iS 00:29:31 RiGHT NOW.    
                                                                   
                                                                   
                        CHOOSE YOUR ACTiON :>


MAYBE SOME USERS DON'T WANT TO SEE THE LOGOFF-MENU. PUHH!!! THAT'S HARD,
BUT NO PROBLEM. WHEN A USER LOGS OFF THE FiRST TiME, THE DOOR WiLL iNFORM
HiM, THAT HE HAS NO CONFiG-FiLE. NOW THE USER CAN TYPE iN 'G W' FROM THE
MAiN-PROMPT AND THEN HE CAN CHOOSE iF HE WANTS TO SEE THE LOGOFF-MENU OR
NOT WHENEVER HE LOGS OFF. iMJG WiLL AUTOMATiCALLY WRiTE A CONFiG-FiLE FOR
EACH USER. iF A USER HAS NO CONFiG-FiLE iMJG WiLL iNFORM HiM.

i ALSO ADDED AN ADDiTiONAL EXTERNAL PROGRAM. ALL OLDER VERSiONS HAVE HAD THE
PROBLEM THAT THE LOGOFF DOOR DiD NOT SHOW THE REAL-ON-LiNE TiME OF A USER
WHEN HE/SHE CHATTED WiTH THE SYSOP. THiS WAS BECAUSE /X STOPS COUNTiNG THE
TiME WHEN A USER ENTERS THE CHAT-MODE WiTH THE SYSOP. WiTH THE SMALL
EXTERNAL PROGRAM iT DOESN'T MATTER. NOW iMJG WiLL SHOW THE CORRECT ONLiNE-
TiME WHEN HE LOGS OFF.

THERE iS ONE SMALL EXCEPTiON. iMJG WiLL NOT SHOW THE REAL ON-LiNE-TiME
iF THE USER WHO LOGS iN DOES NOT PASS THE EXTERNAL TiME-COUNTER. THiS
PROBABLY ONLY MiGHT HAPPEN iF THE SYSOP LOGS iN WiTH A SYSOP-LOGiN AND THE
EXTERNAL PROGRAM iS BUiLT iNTO THE LOGON-SCREEN ViA MCi-COMMANDS. ALL
OTHER WAYS iT WiLL WORK 100%.


AND NOW i THiNK i GAVE YOU ENOUGH REASONS TO iNSTALL iMJG VERSiON 1.5. :)

@ENDNODE

@NODE iNSTALLATiON "iNSTALLATiON OF iMJG VERSiON 1.5"

iNSTALLATiON TO @{"AMi EXPRESS V2.xx" LiNK AMiEXPRESSV2.xx}.

iNSTALLATiON TO @{"AMi EXPRESS V3.xx" LiNK AMiEXPRESSV3.xx}.

@ENDNODE

@NODE AMiEXPRESSV2.xx "iNSTALLATiON TO AMi EXPRESS V2.xx"

TO iNSTALL THE DOOR LOAD UP THE CUSTOMCOMMANDS (/X V2.2x OR BELOW) OR
BBS.CMD (/X V2.3x) AND ADD THE FOLLOWiNG LiNE TO THE LiST.


          11 SPACES iN         
          |
------------------------------------------------          
*G        RM010MODULES:MM_TOOLS/GEHEN/GEHEN.REXX
------------------------------------------------
||        |||  |           
||        |||  ` 'MODULES:MM_TOOLS/GEHEN/GEHEN.REXX' iS THE LOCATiON OF
||        |||     THE FiLE.
||        |||
||        ||` 020 THE MiNiMUM ACCESS TO USE THiS DOOR. CHANGE iT TO WHAT
||        ||      YOU LiKE.
||        ||
||        |` 'M' FOR A MULTiNODE BBS ('S' FOR A SiNGLE NODE BBS).
||        |
||        ` 'R' FOR A REXX DOOR WHiCH WiLL USE THE 'REXXDOOR'-UTiL.
||
|`COMMAND TO START THE DOOR.
|
`-RETARD OPTiON. TO MAKE SURE THEY ONLY USE 'G' & ONLY  'G' TO GET THE
  DOOR TO COME UP. iF NOT USED, THiNGS SUCH AS 'GOOUT' AND 'GA' WOULD
  STiLL BRiNG UP THE DOOR.


  USE THE LiNE BETWEEN THE LiNES ONLY. THE OTHER PARTS ARE JUST AN
  EXPLANATiON TO MAKE SURE YOU KNOW WHAT EACH PART iS DOiNG (SiNCE
  NOONE WOULD TELL ME BACK iN THE DAYS WHERE i DiDN'T KNOW WHAT WAS
  GOiNG ON!)  

  NOW COPY THE 'DODELAY'-COMMAND FROM THE C-DiRECTORY OF THE
  LHA-ARCHiEVE iNTO YOUR C-DiRECTORY.

  NOW COPY THE DiRECTORY 'MODULES' FROM THE LHA-ARCHiEV TO YOUR BBS.

  AT LAST EDiT THE @{"CONFiGFiLES" LiNK CONFiGFiLES}. YOU FiND WiLL THEM iN
 
  'BBS:MODULES/MM_TOOLS/GEHEN'.


  THE VERY LAST THiNG TO DO iS TO iNSTALL THE 'ZEiT.REXX'. THE BEST WAY
  iS TO iT iNTO THE LOGON-SCREEN. HERE COMES HOW iT WORKS.

  ADD THE FOLLOWiNG TO YOUR LOGON.TXT AND LOGON.TXT.GR:


  --------------CUT HERE----------------
  ~CC_ZEiT
  --------------CUT HERE----------------


  TO iNSTALL THE DOOR LOAD UP THE CUSTOMCOMMANDS (/X V2.2x OR BELOW) OR
  SYS.CMD (/X V2.3x) AND ADD THE FOLLOWiNG LiNE TO THE LiST.

          11 SPACES iN         
          |
-----------------------------------------------          
*ZEiT     RM010MODULES:MM_TOOLS/GEHEN/ZEiT.REXX
-----------------------------------------------

  THAT iS ALL...

@ENDNODE

@NODE AMiEXPRESSV3.xx "iNSTALLATiON TO AMi EXPRESS V3.xx"

ADD THE FOLLOWiNG TO YOUR LOGON.TXT AND LOGON.TXT.GR:


--------------CUT HERE----------------
